WEBVTT

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:07.600
<i>My mother left us before I turned ten.</i>

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:11.760
<i>I didn't want to end up like her,</i>

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:20.160
<i>or like my father and grandfather,
who grew overconfident in their abilities.</i>

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:22.570
<i>I wanted to leave home</i>

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:26.210
<i>and pursue a skill that would
mature and refine with age,</i>

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:29.630
<i>or perhaps a career in literature or art.</i>

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:35.150
<i>That's why I decided to walk down
the thorny path of music.</i>

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:08.890
<i>Spring break.</i>

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:12.310
<i>With freshmen numbers dwindling by the year,</i>

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:18.530
<i>we minor culture clubs competed fiercely
to recruit them before the school year even began.</i>

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:20.650
The concert band is waiting for you!

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:23.670
Join now, and you'll get to take
the stage at a competition!

00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:25.330
A boy!

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:26.740
We want boys!

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:29.720
Hold it right there!

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:31.080
If you want members,

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:33.040
you'll have to recruit them over the drama club's dead—

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:38.520
We're the drama club.
Please consider joining us.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:40.030
I'll think about it.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:44.400
Oh, dear.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:44.960
Hey!

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:47.010
What do you guys think you're doing?!

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:12.080
Haruta!

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.140
How'd it go?

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:16.670
Awful.

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:18.910
What in the world did you do?

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:23.300
Weird. Even by myself,
it should've been a piece of cake.

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:26.090
Don't you know how hard we had it last year?

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:31.080
Relax. We'll get loads of girls
joining for you once school begins.

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:32.960
I only like them older.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:35.730
Hey, I like them older too!

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:38.120
At least ten years older, or I'm not interested!

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:42.860
I guess as childhood friends,
we were fated to have similar tastes.

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:44.740
I'd rather we didn't!

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:48.700
Please, go out with a girl who isn't me!

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:50.830
Girls are great, you know!

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.830
What's gotten into you?

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:57.610
What'd you even come here for?

00:03:57.610 --> 00:04:00.840
To show you this. Someone from
the newspaper club gave it to me earlier.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:05.300
Said they took it at around 8AM,
before our practice started.

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:06.970
Look at this.

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:10.080
You can see someone in the music room.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.140
Oh, yeah.

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:17.590
Right? This makes it clear that someone's
sneaking in there before we arrive!

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:18.560
I guess.

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:21.980
Remember the first day of spring break?

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:26.670
When I came to school early
to practise by myself...

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:28.310
Huh?

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:33.370
Good morning!

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:34.750
Huh?

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:36.260
Nobody's here.

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:38.670
Who's there?

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:48.180
Even after that,

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:52.110
there were several days when the keys
were gone from the staff room in the morning.

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:56.260
I would go to the music room
thinking someone had come before me,

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:57.550
only to find it empty.

00:04:57.550 --> 00:05:00.410
Then, finding that weird,
I'd go back to the staff room

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:01.900
and the key would be right there.

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:06.700
So basically, someone was entering and exiting
the music room without ever running into you.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:10.120
That's right! We have a mysterious
trespasser on our hands!

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:12.770
Surely it's just a student.

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:14.490
But it's spring break!

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:17.990
Normal students would be sleeping in at home!

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:21.920
Why would one ever visit the music room
so early in the morning?

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:24.530
Must've had something more
important to do than sleep in.

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:26.210
What's the matter with you?

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:28.550
Don't you sense anything from this?!

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:30.340
Well, uh, I guess...

00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:32.360
Forget it.

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:34.600
I'll go talk to Kusakabe-sensei.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.090
Sorry, Chika-chan.

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:38.320
It's all good. No need to worry.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:44.690
That student is probably a spring mirage to us.

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:47.610
A spring mirage?

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:48.860
Yeah.

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:53.490
As much as we wish for it to stay forever,
it'll end up as but a fleeting pipe dream.

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:58.680
Thanks to you, I think I can solve
the other spring break mystery.

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:14.720
Maren and Narushima-san?

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:17.890
While the choir uses the music room,

00:06:17.890 --> 00:06:21.520
we scatter across the big school campus
and practise by ourselves.

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:26.760
Every now and then, we send out a signal
and break into an impromptu ensemble,

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:30.960
but a certain instrument's been
joining us since yesterday.

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:32.070
What is it?

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:32.950
Just watch.

00:06:57.720 --> 00:06:58.520
Found it!

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:00.870
A clarinet?

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:03.960
Wow, who is that?

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:09.530
Looks like it's a student who's taking
makeups during spring break.

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:12.720
Could she be stupid?

00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:17.430
President.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:21.370
Didn't we have an unused clarinet lying around?

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:23.000
What is this, out of the blue?

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:27.960
It needs to be repaired,
so you can't use it right away.

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:29.130
Okay.

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:30.240
Huh?

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:32.050
It really is gone, huh?

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:34.710
They took it without telling anyone?

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:37.720
Repairing these isn't some DIY job, either.
You need technical expertise.

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:39.640
So who could do it?

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:41.300
Serizawa Naoko, maybe?

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:45.060
Wait, Serizawa? The first year?

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:48.230
If so, her playing was a bit weird.

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:52.290
Yes. Her timing was off at
the start of multiple phrases.

00:07:52.290 --> 00:07:57.240
That reminds me. I saw her with
Kusakabe-sensei before the closing ceremony.

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:58.430
What?

00:07:58.430 --> 00:08:01.490
Time out! Let me in on your conversation!

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:04.160
What do you want to know about Serizawa?

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:06.200
You're familiar with her?

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:09.200
The Serizawas are local celebrities, you know.

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:11.180
Her grandfather was a Diet member,

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:14.140
and her father runs a construction company.

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:16.920
She's a thoroughbred musician
who's looking to go pro.

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:17.890
Go pro?!

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:21.430
Awesome! If someone like that joined—

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:22.480
Forget about it.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:26.990
She's a hardcore concert band hater.

00:08:26.990 --> 00:08:29.400
Talk to her, and you'll get burnt.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:30.610
Burnt?

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:33.980
When my little sister was in the concert band,

00:08:33.980 --> 00:08:36.910
she once went to ask her
to fill in and came back crying.

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:42.020
N-Nobody who loves music
could ever hate concert bands...

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:44.210
Probably... Maybe...

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:49.470
A lot of aspiring pros consider
music a personal battle.

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:50.380
So?

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:56.170
A concert band could have members who
only picked up an instrument in high school,

00:08:56.170 --> 00:08:59.220
so they consider practising
with one a waste of time.

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:01.130
Does it burn?

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:02.760
N-Not in the least!

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:08.600
There are also people who can't stand being
lumped in with players far worse than them.

00:09:08.600 --> 00:09:11.560
What's the big deal?
We could all level up together.

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:14.400
Want me to put it in RPG terms, then?

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:17.600
Let's say you're a level 1 performer.

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:20.740
Kamijou, Narushima, and Maren would be level 50.

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:24.120
And Serizawa would be level 99.

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:28.770
She's been working several times harder
than you ever since grade school.

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:31.250
I might get burnt to a crisp.

00:09:32.150 --> 00:09:35.840
Why would you guys play
with me if you're so good?

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:39.430
I like playing in a concert band
because it lets me play with friends.

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:41.820
There's more to music than just being good.

00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:44.070
And nothing beats concert bands
when it comes to fun.

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:46.390
You won't regret it!

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:47.990
I'll do my best!

00:09:47.990 --> 00:09:53.230
I'll recruit more members and make sure we can
take part in the Category A local qualifiers!

00:09:54.770 --> 00:09:56.530
All right. My HP is restored.

00:09:56.530 --> 00:09:58.740
Man, you're easy to please.

00:09:59.190 --> 00:10:05.160
Oh yeah, I heard Serizawa-san's grades fell off
a cliff starting from the second midterms.

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:08.000
Before that, she was in the top five of our year.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:09.580
Is that why she has to take makeups?

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:12.040
That probably has more to do
with her attendance.

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:14.560
She suddenly started having trouble
following conversations,

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:17.460
began to avoid her classmates,
and ended up cut off from the rest.

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:20.520
Due to that, she took most of the third term off.

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:26.940
Haruta, you saw her and
Kusakabe-sensei talking alone, right?

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:27.880
I did.

00:10:27.880 --> 00:10:30.950
I saw them going into the career
counselling room multiple times.

00:10:30.950 --> 00:10:32.280
Career counselling?

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:33.150
Multiple times?!

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:35.440
Her, of all people?

00:10:36.670 --> 00:10:40.280
How did you conveniently end up
witnessing that each time?

00:10:40.280 --> 00:10:44.050
I can't relax unless I see Sensei's
face multiple times a day.

00:10:44.050 --> 00:10:45.280
You stole another march on me?!

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:52.250
You're her!

00:10:53.070 --> 00:10:54.290
Serizawa-san?

00:11:03.030 --> 00:11:04.880
It really has been repaired.

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:06.760
Where's my thanks?

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:07.760
P...

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:08.620
P?

00:11:08.970 --> 00:11:10.350
Please join our band!

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:12.140
Wh-What's with you?!

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:15.450
I love how audacious you are.

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:19.230
So why did I bother explaining all that before?

00:11:19.730 --> 00:11:21.760
You're Homura-san, of Class 1-2?

00:11:22.460 --> 00:11:27.210
Over the past year, the nearly-dead concert band
came back to life with you at its core.

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:29.290
You've got a keen eye.

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:32.960
You even battled the drama club
on stage in the gym.

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:34.010
You saw that?!

00:11:34.010 --> 00:11:37.920
But I've known of you since long before that.

00:11:38.970 --> 00:11:41.790
Don't you remember what happened last summer?

00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:47.200
She came to school by car and nearly
ran you over in front of the main gate.

00:11:50.470 --> 00:11:51.230
Hup!

00:11:52.810 --> 00:11:53.960
That was you?

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:55.480
Don't be like that, Chika-chan.

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:59.560
You already accepted the expensive
cream bun settlement offered by the driver.

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:02.110
Oh, right.

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:08.590
Um, thanks for repairing it.

00:12:09.870 --> 00:12:12.330
I'm not going to join, sorry.

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:13.240
Join?

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:15.830
What's wrong?

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:20.420
Wait. You came all the way,
so let's talk some more.

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:21.430
I'm sorry!

00:12:22.530 --> 00:12:24.990
What did she even come here to do?

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:30.770
I think we'd all better watch our step.

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:32.250
Our step?

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:37.890
She probably lost something in
the music room or this prep room.

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:39.810
Think she dropped a contact lens?

00:12:39.810 --> 00:12:42.640
No, but it's probably something similar...

00:12:42.640 --> 00:12:45.400
and far more serious.

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:48.880
If she wanted to look for it between
the choir and concert band's practices,

00:12:48.880 --> 00:12:50.200
the morning was her only option.

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:52.990
But she soon hit a wall looking by herself.

00:12:52.990 --> 00:12:55.800
Maybe she snuck out the clarinet and repaired it

00:12:55.800 --> 00:13:00.670
so she wouldn't owe us anything
for our help with the search.

00:13:01.580 --> 00:13:02.460
Don't tell me...

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:07.100
Our conversation went awry the moment
the choir started practising.

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:12.000
I'll go bring her back!

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:12.850
Chika?!

00:13:13.790 --> 00:13:17.250
<i>Her sudden inability to keep up
with conversations, maintain her grades,</i>

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:19.700
<i>get the timing right at the start of phrases,</i>

00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:22.560
<i>and the career counselling with
Kusakabe-sensei all points to one thing...</i>

00:13:22.560 --> 00:13:23.950
Serizawa-san!

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:28.490
What is it?

00:13:29.190 --> 00:13:32.330
Did you lose your hearing?

00:13:36.220 --> 00:13:38.280
Sudden sensorineural hearing loss?

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:41.290
I've gone completely deaf in my right ear.

00:13:41.290 --> 00:13:43.040
And my left's gotten to the point

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:48.150
where it's hard for me to pick up everyday
conversation unless I'm in a quiet place.

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:51.090
I'm receiving treatment, but...

00:13:56.190 --> 00:13:59.040
I played volleyball in junior high.

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:02.360
One of my teammates got hit
in the ear with a really hard spike.

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:06.400
We were competing for
a starting spot at the time,

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:08.930
but she eventually lost out.

00:14:08.930 --> 00:14:13.240
After that, she started mishearing things
more frequently, even in daily life.

00:14:13.670 --> 00:14:15.680
I saw her crying and—

00:14:15.680 --> 00:14:18.120
What does that have to do with me?

00:14:18.860 --> 00:14:20.120
Everything!

00:14:21.180 --> 00:14:22.920
Could you be any more abrasive?

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:24.820
I don't want your stupid sympathy.

00:14:24.820 --> 00:14:29.600
Why would I ever pity a brilliant,
level 99 rich girl?

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:37.590
Oh, I know!

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:40.270
Don't move out of line!

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:43.230
It's really small, so be sure not to miss it!

00:14:44.310 --> 00:14:46.780
Quit slacking off, Prez. Hold the other side!

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:51.200
That took a while.

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:54.940
She came sprinting after me.
I had a hard time dealing with her.

00:14:54.940 --> 00:14:56.640
Doesn't seem to be in the music room!

00:14:56.640 --> 00:14:59.150
Let's look in the prep room, then.

00:14:59.150 --> 00:15:02.950
Hurry up and tell everyone what size and colour it is.

00:15:02.950 --> 00:15:05.530
Around the size of a pinky nail. Skin tone.

00:15:05.530 --> 00:15:07.050
That small?

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:10.220
And it rolls around. Better not kick it.

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:12.640
That doesn't sound easy to find at all.

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:14.060
Nice idea.

00:15:14.060 --> 00:15:17.410
Thanks. We got the paper cups from the infirmary.

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:19.220
These aren't half-bad.

00:15:19.220 --> 00:15:22.120
I can even talk to people in noisy places.

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:23.660
Finally found it.

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:25.900
He says they found it.

00:15:27.370 --> 00:15:30.320
Don't be in such a rush, now.

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:34.080
Tell her everything I'm about to say.

00:15:35.550 --> 00:15:39.400
The concert band members
gave it their all for over an hour.

00:15:39.400 --> 00:15:41.510
It was one hell of a workout.

00:15:42.220 --> 00:15:44.230
We deserve praise for that, really.

00:15:44.230 --> 00:15:47.920
Apparently he wants to run for
student council president this year.

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:50.430
Oh? Then you have my vote.

00:15:50.430 --> 00:15:51.510
Your vote?

00:15:51.510 --> 00:15:53.530
Chika-chan, are you really
telling her what I said?

00:15:53.530 --> 00:15:56.010
I am. Now get on with it.

00:15:57.440 --> 00:16:00.180
This was an unfortunate accident.

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:01.270
Accident?

00:16:01.270 --> 00:16:04.600
So nobody should be blamed for it.

00:16:15.500 --> 00:16:17.820
I never thought you'd be such a pain.

00:16:17.820 --> 00:16:21.020
Why didn't you tell us sooner?

00:16:21.020 --> 00:16:25.150
If not us, you could've at least
told Kusakabe-sensei.

00:16:25.150 --> 00:16:26.880
I couldn't possibly tell him.

00:16:27.350 --> 00:16:30.000
Not after all the trouble I caused him
with the career counselling.

00:16:30.750 --> 00:16:33.550
I figured it'd be hard for you to
tell them about the hearing aid,

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:36.540
so I called your family and let them know.

00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:38.470
Thank you.

00:16:38.840 --> 00:16:40.820
What are the others up to?

00:16:40.820 --> 00:16:42.590
Tending to the instruments.

00:16:42.590 --> 00:16:45.770
We did find a bunch of them
that still seemed usable.

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:47.530
It's all thanks to you, Serizawa-san.

00:16:47.530 --> 00:16:50.270
If only you'd repair the rest for free, too.

00:16:50.270 --> 00:16:52.800
She can't do everything, you know.

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:56.770
Sorry. I can't handle all of you
talking to me at once.

00:16:56.770 --> 00:16:57.670
All done!

00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:05.490
There.

00:17:05.930 --> 00:17:07.630
Now we can all talk to her.

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:11.710
You're sharing mine, okay?

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:13.880
Be careful not to let the strings loosen.

00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:16.560
Mind if I ask you something?

00:17:16.950 --> 00:17:17.930
What is it?

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:20.790
What made you pick up clarinet?

00:17:21.960 --> 00:17:28.350
My father's introduced me to a lot of aspiring
pro musicians ever since I was young.

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:32.150
But not one of them played the clarinet.

00:17:33.290 --> 00:17:36.010
That was probably just bad luck.

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:39.510
As for me, it was anything goes.

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:44.220
All I cared about was becoming a
pro musician and leaving that house.

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:47.160
That's all, really.

00:17:47.160 --> 00:17:49.430
Leave that palace you call a home?!

00:17:49.430 --> 00:17:52.220
What a waste! You could be a NEET there forever!

00:17:52.220 --> 00:17:53.380
President!

00:17:55.360 --> 00:17:56.440
Serizawa-san.

00:17:57.480 --> 00:18:00.230
How does our band look from your point of view?

00:18:02.390 --> 00:18:05.230
You've accomplished nothing worth mentioning,

00:18:05.230 --> 00:18:08.950
and you haven't even taken
the shape of a proper band yet.

00:18:08.950 --> 00:18:10.400
Tell us something we don't know.

00:18:12.030 --> 00:18:15.560
Don't tell me, you're seriously aiming for Fumon Hall?

00:18:15.560 --> 00:18:16.680
Yeah.

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:19.490
Then...

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:21.690
Sensei must've found it
hard to break this to you,

00:18:21.690 --> 00:18:24.110
but I'll say it for him now.

00:18:25.070 --> 00:18:26.960
You need at least thirty members.

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:28.650
Thirty?

00:18:28.650 --> 00:18:34.100
In the high-school Category-A All-Japans,
they call you rash if you take part with thirty.

00:18:34.100 --> 00:18:35.420
Any lower,

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:39.600
and there'll be a clear gap between you and the
powerhouse bands with the maximum fifty-five members.

00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:40.270
Wait.

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:42.840
There is a way to close that gap.

00:18:42.840 --> 00:18:44.440
Orchestral reduction, right?

00:18:44.950 --> 00:18:49.100
Arranging full symphony music for a smaller band
to surprise pro judges and make an impact.

00:18:49.950 --> 00:18:53.310
This school has an instructor capable of that.

00:18:53.990 --> 00:18:57.740
An instructor who was once called
Japanese music's wunderkind.

00:18:58.110 --> 00:19:01.150
But that won't change the fact
that you'll be at a disadvantage.

00:19:01.930 --> 00:19:04.000
Also, you should give up
on this year's nationals.

00:19:05.110 --> 00:19:07.740
Instead of suffering a crushing defeat
due to lack of members,

00:19:07.740 --> 00:19:09.490
you'd be better off entering Category B

00:19:09.490 --> 00:19:12.500
with its thirty-five member limit
and free-choice pieces only.

00:19:13.120 --> 00:19:14.980
You won't make it to Fumon Hall that way,

00:19:14.980 --> 00:19:17.920
but you can aim for gold
in the Category B regionals,

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:19.870
and gain more valuable experience that way.

00:19:21.670 --> 00:19:25.530
So we have to pave the way for
Kamijou and our other juniors, right?

00:19:26.220 --> 00:19:27.690
Category B...

00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:31.520
You're an amusing one, Kamijou-kun.

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:37.410
I thought Homura-san would be the only one
to have "Join us" written all over her face,

00:19:37.410 --> 00:19:38.590
but you're the same.

00:19:39.190 --> 00:19:40.440
You're like two peas in a pod.

00:19:40.440 --> 00:19:41.730
No way!

00:19:43.110 --> 00:19:44.030
Hey...

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:48.010
Could you help us in our efforts?

00:19:48.880 --> 00:19:50.210
Consider it a request from me too.

00:19:54.510 --> 00:19:55.290
Sensei.

00:19:56.450 --> 00:19:59.640
You gave up on becoming a conductor, right?

00:20:01.120 --> 00:20:07.810
So why do you still surround yourself with music
by teaching at this remote public school?

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:11.750
Music is all I know,

00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:13.600
so I cling to it.

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:16.190
I'm the same.

00:20:16.910 --> 00:20:19.950
The door hasn't been completely shut
on my going professional.

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:24.310
I have to cling to the path I have chosen

00:20:24.310 --> 00:20:27.310
and keep pushing on until I'm satisfied.

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:30.620
Isn't it the same for you all?

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:35.450
So I'm sorry,

00:20:36.360 --> 00:20:38.690
but I can't join you yet.

00:20:39.890 --> 00:20:43.340
There's one thing I just don't
understand from this case.

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:44.640
What?

00:20:44.640 --> 00:20:48.750
How'd you lose your hearing aid
in the music prep room?

00:20:48.750 --> 00:20:52.750
I wanted to check if the snare drums
and timpani were still usable,

00:20:52.750 --> 00:20:54.280
so I picked them up to move them,

00:20:54.870 --> 00:20:56.730
but then I lost my balance and fell.

00:20:57.140 --> 00:20:58.640
Who's there?

00:20:58.640 --> 00:21:00.800
That must've been when it fell out.

00:21:00.800 --> 00:21:04.700
I didn't realise because I was in such a rush.

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:06.970
Why check the snare drums and timpani?

00:21:07.770 --> 00:21:09.490
For a childhood friend.

00:21:10.190 --> 00:21:12.640
I want him to come back to school.

00:21:12.640 --> 00:21:14.040
He plays the drums?

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:16.660
Forget I said anything.

00:21:16.660 --> 00:21:21.290
He must be going through a lot,
and I'm sure he'd hate people meddling.

00:21:26.550 --> 00:21:28.530
Sorry for causing such a fuss.

00:21:28.530 --> 00:21:30.730
I'll be rooting for you from the outside.

00:21:30.730 --> 00:21:32.730
Oh, can I have those?

00:21:38.850 --> 00:21:39.810
Thanks!

00:21:43.940 --> 00:21:47.030
I don't care if she's a prodigy or whatever.

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:49.860
She's just a troublemaker, if you ask me.

00:21:49.860 --> 00:21:50.920
Yet...

00:21:51.780 --> 00:21:54.920
She said she couldn't join us "just yet".

00:21:55.740 --> 00:21:56.870
Yeah.

00:21:57.790 --> 00:22:00.020
A spring mirage, huh?

00:23:31.560 --> 00:23:33.050
I'm here to confess today.

00:23:33.050 --> 00:23:34.050
Be a man and admit it.

00:23:34.050 --> 00:23:35.800
I'm gonna go all the way!

00:23:35.800 --> 00:23:37.970
Our next caller is "Desert Rabbit".

00:23:38.420 --> 00:23:40.480
What's in a name?
